---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
---

<Layout title="About">
  <Nav />
  <section class="section about-page">
    <div class="container about-shell">
      <header class="about-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>

        <h1 class="about-title">
          Hi, I’m Ryan Laird.
        </h1>

        <p class="about-lead">
          I’m a digital developer and science communicator building accessible,
          data-driven web experiences with Astro, React, TypeScript, and Python.
          I care about clear communication, inclusive design, and making complex
          ideas feel understandable.
        </p>

        <div class="badge-row" aria-label="Profile badges">
          <img
            src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Role-Digital%20Developer-7c3aed?style=for-the-badge&logo=code&logoColor=white"
            alt="Role: Digital Developer"
          />
          <img
            src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Stack-Astro%20%7C%20React%20%7C%20TypeScript-0f766e?style=for-the-badge&logo=astro&logoColor=white"
            alt="Stack: Astro, React, TypeScript"
          />
          <img
            src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Focus-Accessibility%20%26%20Inclusive%20Design-2563eb?style=for-the-badge&logo=accessibility&logoColor=white"
            alt="Focus: Accessibility and Inclusive Design"
          />
          <img
            src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Location-UK-111827?style=for-the-badge&logo=unitedkingdom&logoColor=white"
            alt="Location: UK"
          />
        </div>

        <div class="badge-row secondary" aria-label="Professional badges">
          <a href="https://github.com/rjmlaird" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            <img
              src="https://img.shields.io/badge/GitHub-rjmlaird-181717?style=for-the-badge&logo=github&logoColor=white"
              alt="GitHub profile"
            />
          </a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            <img
              src="https://img.shields.io/badge/LinkedIn-Profile-0A66C2?style=for-the-badge&logo=linkedin&logoColor=white"
              alt="LinkedIn profile"
            />
          </a>
          <a href="https://astro.build/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            <img
              src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Builder-Astro-BC52EE?style=for-the-badge&logo=astro&logoColor=white"
              alt="Astro"
            />
          </a>
          <a href="https://react.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            <img
              src="https://img.shields.io/badge/UI-React-61DAFB?style=for-the-badge&logo=react&logoColor=111827"
              alt="React"
            />
          </a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="readme-card">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          I build websites and content systems that balance design, performance,
          and maintainability. My work often spans frontend development,
          structured content, automation, API integration, and science-focused
          communication.
        </p>
        <p>
          I like projects where the details matter: semantic HTML, clean data
          models, accessible components, and enough visual polish to make the
          whole thing feel considered.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="readme-grid">
        <article class="readme-card">
          <h2>What I work on</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Astro and React sites with reusable component systems.</li>
            <li>TypeScript-backed content pipelines and structured schemas.</li>
            <li>API integrations for project, CV, and research data.</li>
            <li>Automation for content syncing, assets, and research workflows.</li>
            <li>Accessible interfaces and clearer digital communication.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="readme-card">
          <h2>Current interests</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Science communication, especially space and climate topics.</li>
            <li>Front-end architecture and maintainable design systems.</li>
            <li>Open source tooling, productivity scripts, and data enrichment.</li>
            <li>Cooking, meal planning, and practical vegetarian recipes.</li>
            <li>Better ways to present technical and scientific information.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="readme-card">
        <h2>Tooling</h2>
        <div class="badge-cloud" aria-label="Tool badges">
          <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Astro-BC52EE?style=for-the-badge&logo=astro&logoColor=white" alt="Astro" />
          <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/React-61DAFB?style=for-the-badge&logo=react&logoColor=111827" alt="React" />
          <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/TypeScript-3178C6?style=for-the-badge&logo=typescript&logoColor=white" alt="TypeScript" />
          <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/JavaScript-F7DF1E?style=for-the-badge&logo=javascript&logoColor=111827" alt="JavaScript" />
          <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3776AB?style=for-the-badge&logo=python&logoColor=white" alt="Python" />
          <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Node.js-339933?style=for-the-badge&logo=node.js&logoColor=white" alt="Node.js" />
          <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/pnpm-F69220?style=for-the-badge&logo=pnpm&logoColor=white" alt="pnpm" />
          <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/GitHub%20Actions-2088FF?style=for-the-badge&logo=githubactions&logoColor=white" alt="GitHub Actions" />
          <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Cloudflare%20Workers-F38020?style=for-the-badge&logo=cloudflare&logoColor=white" alt="Cloudflare Workers" />
          <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Zotero-CC2936?style=for-the-badge&logo=zotero&logoColor=white" alt="Zotero" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="readme-card">
        <h2>Values</h2>
        <p>
          I try to build work that is useful, legible, and welcoming. That means
          thoughtful copy, strong hierarchy, reliable patterns, and a focus on
          accessibility from the start rather than as an afterthought.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also value systems that are easy to maintain over time. Good tooling
          should make the work smoother, not more fragile.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="readme-card">
        <h2>Now</h2>
        <p>
          I’m refining my personal and professional web presence, building
          project showcases, and keeping my content workflow modular so it can
          grow with me.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 7vw, 7rem);
  }

  .about-shell {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-hero {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: 78rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    opacity: 0.72;
  }

  .about-title {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4.8vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
  }

  .about-lead {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 72ch;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    opacity: 0.94;
  }

  .badge-row,
  .badge-cloud {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .badge-row img,
  .badge-cloud img {
    display: block;
    height: 28px;
    width: auto;
  }

  .badge-row.secondary {
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .readme-card {
    padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 1.3rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 12%, transpa
